      <tei:div type="colophon" subtype="notes">
        <tei:p>Alice Lucas’s rhymed paraliturgical translation of the piyyut “Hamavdil Ben Ḳodesh l’Ḥol” (the separation between the Holy and Mundane) by Yitsḥaq ben Yehudah ibn Ghayyat, was first published in her <tei:hi rend="italic">Songs of Zion</tei:hi> (1894), pages 53-55, under the title “Hymn for the Conclusion of the Sabbath.” The piyyut was originally composed for the Yom Kippur neilah service.</tei:p>
        <tei:p>Thanks to Nir Krakauer for identifying the piyyut from Lucas’s English verse. For the Hebrew source, I chose the text from Rabbi Simeon Singer’s <tei:hi rend="italic">Authorised Daily Prayer Book</tei:hi> (1890), as it seems very close to the girsah Lucas translated from, albeit with a stanza she left untranslated. –Aharon Varady</tei:p>
      </tei:div>
      <j:endConditional target="#osp_36163_notes"/>
